Requirements: 22   with obligations: 21   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] An obligation is attributed to the requirement its quoted text comes from.
    -> attribute-obligation-by-quoted-text-span  [invariant/explicit]
       An obligation is attributed to the requirement whose span contains the quoted
       text it derives from.

[constraint-01] An obligation carries a quotation of the task text it derives from.
    -> obligation-carries-task-text-quotation  [invariant/explicit]
       An obligation carries a quotation of the task text it derives from.

[constraint-02] An obligation's quotation is located within the span of the requirement
    the obligation is attributed to, not merely somewhere in the task file.
    -> obligation-quotation-within-requirement-span  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves constraint-06)
       An obligation's quotation is located within the span of the requirement the
       obligation is attributed to, not merely somewhere in the task file.

[constraint-03] An obligation whose quotation falls outside the span of the requirement
    it was attributed to is re-attributed to the requirement whose span contains the
    quotation.
    -> obligation-reattribute-out-of-span-quotation  [functional/explicit]
       An obligation whose quotation falls outside the span of the requirement it was
       attributed to is re-attributed to the requirement whose span contains the
       quotation.

[constraint-04] An obligation whose quotation matches no requirement's span is recorded
    as an answer that could not be used, and no requirement is left claiming it.
    -> obligation-unmatched-quotation-recorded-unused  [error_handling/explicit]
       An obligation whose quotation matches no requirement's span is recorded as an
       answer that could not be used, and no requirement is left claiming it.

[constraint-05] Re-attributing an obligation leaves the obligation's own content
    unchanged.
    -> obligation-reattribution-preserves-content  [invariant/explicit]
       Re-attributing an obligation leaves the obligation's own content unchanged.

[constraint-06] A requirement keeps every obligation whose quotation lies within its
    span.
    -> obligation-quotation-within-requirement-span  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves constraint-02)
       An obligation's quotation is located within the span of the requirement the
       obligation is attributed to, not merely somewhere in the task file.

[constraint-07] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
    state.
    -> obligation-byte-identical-review-state  [regression/explicit]
       Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review state.

[constraint-08] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> obligation-tests-no-live-model-calls  [docs_config/explicit]
       Tests issue no live model calls.

